  "text": "France became more threatening, while Argentina’s attack faded after Di María went off. Before Acuña replaced him, Argentina were still producing chances; immediately afterward, they managed 0 shots while France began testing the goal. That suggests a loss of attacking outlet, although the substitution alone cannot explain the shift. [[ev:sb:3869685:2355]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2204]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2517]]\n\nFrance’s later introductions of Camavinga and Coman were followed by a much sharper comeback. It was not simply sustained possession dominance, the passing share became almost even, but France made their attacks count: Mbappé scored the penalty and then the equaliser. The changes coincided with France becoming more dangerous, rather than proving they caused it. [[ev:sb:3869685:2660]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2661]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2928]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2987]]",
